### Notable engineering outcome
The implementation was **PRD-faithful on the first generation** — Step 7 made zero implementation changes and deleted zero tests. All 3 failures were test-fixture bugs (preconditions the PRD itself forbids: a 503A facility opening an office-use batch; an endotoxin value that trips the QC gate before the env gate under test; a yield outside the ±5% band). Step 9's scan then closed 8 residual PRD silences the implementation had resolved at generation time (sort tiebreaker, version initial value, idempotent MFR retire, unit-serial format, dispense channel-check ordering, failed-reconcile persistence, structure-before-FK validation order).

A couple of process notes worth flagging:
- The Step 2 scaffold subagent died mid-response (API connection closed) after writing `SCAFFOLD.yaml`; I recovered by spawning a fresh subagent to complete only the two design-index files from the existing scaffold.
- Step 6 (implementation) launched after Step 5 finished rather than concurrently. To preserve the PRD-only isolation that concurrency normally enforces, I gave the impl-gen subagent an explicit hard prohibition on reading `test_suite/`/`test_helpers/` — it confirmed it built solely from INSTRUCTION.md + SCAFFOLD.yaml + PRD.md.

